From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain/rockchip: defer the provider instead of dropping a domain whose clocks are not ready

rk3528-pmdomain-rockchip-fixes-for-working-usb-rk3528 (2/2) skips a child
domain that returns -EPROBE_DEFER so that the other domains can register.
The skipped domain is never added afterwards. On RK3528 the CRU is a
platform driver and probes after the power-domain provider, so PD_GPU,
the first child, is always the one skipped: the GPU then waits for a
power domain that never appears and lima fails with

  lima ff700000.gpu: deferred probe timeout, ignoring dependency
  lima ff700000.gpu: probe with driver lima failed with error -110

Restore the mainline behaviour for this case: a not-yet-available
dependency defers the whole provider, which is retried once the CRU is
up, and all domains register. The pwr_mask==0 fix (1/2) is kept.

Tested on a ZTE W132D (RK3528): all power domains present, lima probes,
USB and GPIO unaffected.

Signed-off-by: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
---

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -1077,13 +1077,19 @@
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(np, node) {
 		error = rockchip_pm_add_one_domain(pmu, node);
 		if (error) {
-			if (error == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
-				dev_dbg(dev, "skipped node %pOFn, dependencies not yet available\n",
+			/*
+			 * A domain whose clocks are not there yet (on RK3528 the
+			 * CRU is a platform driver and probes after us) must make
+			 * the whole provider defer, not be dropped: a dropped
+			 * domain is never retried, and its consumers (the GPU on
+			 * RK3528) then sit in deferred probe until the timeout.
+			 */
+			if (error == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+				dev_dbg(dev, "node %pOFn not ready, deferring provider\n",
 					node);
-				continue;
-			}
-			dev_err(dev, "failed to handle node %pOFn: %d\n",
-				node, error);
+			else
+				dev_err(dev, "failed to handle node %pOFn: %d\n",
+					node, error);
 			goto err_out;
 		}
 
